# Cache-Control for the Eddie runtime on Cloudflare Pages or Netlify: copy
# this file to your site's static/ directory (it is served as /_headers).
#
# Two independent `?v=` values, so a content deploy does not re-download the
# engine:
#
#   the runtime assets (eddie-widget.js, eddie-worker.js, eddie-sw-*.js,
#   eddie-lite.wasm, eddie-dense.wasm and the wasm glue) carry
#   ?v=<asset hash>, stamped into every bundle by widget/build.sh from the
#   files that produced them. It changes when Eddie is upgraded, not when
#   the site is rebuilt.
#
#   index.ed, its index.<lane>.ed sidecars and models/<lane>/* carry
#   ?v=<index hash> from the Hugo partial. Those really are rebuilt together.
#
# Both hosts match rules on the path only; the query string is part of the
# browser's and the CDN's cache key, which is what makes ?v= work with
# `immutable`.
#
# eddie-boot.js is the one URL the page references without a ?v=, so it is
# the one that should keep revalidating: it carries the asset hash the rest
# of the runtime is fetched with.
#
# Two things measured on Cloudflare Pages (www.jason-grey.com, 2026-09-01)
# that the rules below cannot get around:
#
#   Pages MERGES the directives of every matching rule rather than letting a
#   later rule replace an earlier one, so `immutable` from the wildcard
#   reaches eddie-boot.js too. Naming the long-lived files one per line
#   instead of using the wildcard was worse: `immutable` was then dropped
#   from all of them.
#
#   The zone's Browser Cache TTL wins over a smaller max-age here, so the
#   300 below came back as 14400.
#
# The result on that zone is `max-age=14400, immutable, must-revalidate` for
# the loader: an Eddie upgrade reaches a returning visitor within four hours
# rather than five minutes. Everything else is correctly immutable, which is
# the part that matters. Set Browser Cache TTL to "Respect Existing Headers"
# in the Cloudflare dashboard if you want the five minutes.

/eddie/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/eddie/eddie-boot.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

# With `loader = "full"` the page references eddie-widget.js directly, again
# without a ?v=, so it needs the same treatment -- and then it revalidates on
# every visit instead of being fetched once. That is the trade the boot
# loader exists to avoid; uncomment only if you set loader = "full".
#
# /eddie/eddie-widget.js
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
